# The assessment of AGT-011 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity
# is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record
# registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# AGT-011: "KnowledgeSourceRole values shall include at minimum NormativeRepositoryPolicy,
# ApprovedArchitectureDecision, ImplementationDocumentation, CodeOrTestEvidence,
# RuntimeOrBenchmarkObservation, ExternalReference, HistoricalRationale, and
# AgentGeneratedInterpretation. Evidence classification, confidence, semantic similarity,
# and source role shall remain separate dimensions."
#
# `KnowledgeSourceRole` and its eight named values do not exist as a real type anywhere --
# only as corpus/roadmap text in spec-ingest and spec-model test fixtures.
#
# The requirement's second sentence -- evidence classification, confidence, and source role
# shall remain separate dimensions -- is already real and deliberately enforced for the two
# dimensions Nomos does have: `EvidenceClass`'s own doc comment states it is "deliberately
# not reducible to one confidence number. A prediction at 0.9 and a measurement at 0.9 are
# not interchangeable," and its combinator is tested to never manufacture a scalar strength;
# `Confidence` is a distinct bounded newtype in a different crate and band (`nomos-model`,
# kernel) from `EvidenceClass` (`nomos-contracts`, band 0), so the two cannot be collapsed
# into one field by construction. Source role itself is simply absent, not collapsed into
# either -- there is no third dimension yet to keep separate.
verdict: Partial
